  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43341022",
      "title": "Loading Unknown Images",
      "lectureOrder": 198,
      "videoOrder": 184,
      "sourceHash": "d4f89da1561c1d540696a4018c34fbb95358af528adec94127dfac9ce7996a39",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 2.04,
          "en": "So let's now work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 6.03,
          "en": "on optimizing these user-generated images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 7.92,
          "en": "And one problem we'll have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "is that we don't know the size of the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 14.7,
          "en": "that have been uploaded by the users in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.7,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "but I'll of course show you how to work around that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "Now let's start by going to the post component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "where we output those images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 26.28,
          "en": "And of course we can start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.28,
          "end": 29.46,
          "en": "by also using the NextJS image component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.46,
          "end": 33.03,
          "en": "instead of the native built-in image element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "For that, you must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 36.72,
          "en": "that you import that component though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.72,
          "end": 40.023,
          "en": "so that you import image from next image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.7,
          "end": 43.77,
          "en": "Now, if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.77,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "and you would save the code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 47.46,
          "en": "you would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.46,
          "end": 48.87,
          "en": "and you would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 53.46,
          "en": "because of course, we're now setting a string path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.46,
          "end": 56.19,
          "en": "as the source for our image component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.19,
          "end": 59.58,
          "en": "And as you saw before, that doesn't work like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.58,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "Instead, this image component wants an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 67.23,
          "en": "as a value for the source prop, or does it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 70.23,
          "en": "Well, actually it needs such an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.23,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "if you're not setting a width and height manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 76.5,
          "en": "But if you do set width and height props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.5,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "on the next image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 82.08,
          "en": "you can indeed use a string path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.08,
          "end": 85.92,
          "en": "Now, the width and height you do set here could be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.92,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "to size the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 89.28,
          "en": "and you could therefore set width and height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.28,
          "end": 93,
          "en": "to the sizes you wanna display the image at,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 96.93,
          "en": "but that's actually not how you should use these props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.93,
          "end": 98.46000000000001,
          "en": "As I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.46000000000001,
          "end": 100.68,
          "en": "whilst you can do it as a workaround,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.68,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "it's not the recommended way of using width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 108.87,
          "en": "Instead, you should normally set the native raw width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.87,
          "end": 111.39,
          "en": "and height of the input image here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.39,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "And of course, we don't know that if the image was chosen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 116.85300000000001,
          "en": "and uploaded by a user of our website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.96000000000001,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "Therefore, what NextJS offers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 123.45,
          "en": "as an alternative in situations like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 126.813,
          "en": "is that you set the fill prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.89,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "And you can simply add it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 131.88,
          "en": "and therefore set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.88,
          "end": 136.5,
          "en": "If you do that, you'll see that we still get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.5,
          "end": 138.32999999999998,
          "en": "but now it's a different error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.94,
          "en": "that essentially this host name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 144.57,
          "en": "from which we're trying to fetch the image is not configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.57,
          "end": 147.48,
          "en": "under images in our next config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.48,
          "end": 149.793,
          "en": "So what's this error about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "Well, whenever you are loading an image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 156.27,
          "en": "from an external site, as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 160.98,
          "en": "NextJS for security reasons, blocks that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.98,
          "end": 163.92000000000002,
          "en": "and gives you that error instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.92000000000002,
          "end": 166.44,
          "en": "But of course, here we wanna load the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.44,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "from that remote site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "and therefore what we have to do is we have to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 172.47,
          "en": "to this next.config file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "and unlock this specific external site, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 179.973,
          "en": "to allow loading images from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.84,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "And you do that by adding the images property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 186.813,
          "en": "to this configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.86,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "and you set this to an object itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 195.98,
          "en": "And then in there you can add the remotePatterns setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 198,
          "en": "and set this to an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198,
          "end": 202.07999999999998,
          "en": "of remote host addresses you wanna allow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.07999999999998,
          "end": 206.073,
          "en": "for loading images in your NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.91,
          "end": 210.15,
          "en": "Now, remotePatterns actually wants an array of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.15,
          "end": 213.48,
          "en": "and in every object you can then set up a host name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.48,
          "end": 215.64,
          "en": "So the domain name in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.64,
          "end": 218.97,
          "en": "of these external sites you wanna allow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.97,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "In my case here, res.cloudinary.com,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 226.41,
          "en": "that is the domain with which all those links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.41,
          "end": 229.263,
          "en": "to the Cloudinary hosted images will start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.2,
          "en": "By adding this configuration setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.2,
          "end": 234.32999999999998,
          "en": "and then saving this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 237.39,
          "en": "you will see that if you now reload, this error goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.39,
          "end": 239.49,
          "en": "But now I got large images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "which take up the entire size of the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 246.87,
          "en": "And that's happening because of this fill prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.87,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "And it's of course not the behavior we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 250.653,
          "en": "so let's work on that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
